			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Add ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform plugin\n\nUpdate Element submodule to pull in new ESBuild transform plugin that exposes VS Code's IInstantiationService and IWorkbench facade on globalThis. The transform patches web.main.js to stash IInstantiationService after workbench.startup() and web.factory.js to expose the IWorkbench facade after workbenchPromise.complete(). Both injections are idempotent, short-circuiting on existing markers.\n\nThis enables Sky-side bridge code to resolve internal VS Code services via __CEL_INSTANTIATION_SERVICE.invokeFunction(), allowing proper integration of extension-contributed UI elements like status bar items and SCM providers without re-implementing parallel UI surfaces.",
			"SHA": "45b2541a478d94e694610be813fdfd6011787e9b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T01:24:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				5213,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Update Element submodule with workspace folders, status bar removal, SCM events\n\nSynchronize Element submodule reference from 31cf2b5f to 21ddbb2. This pulls in coordinated changes across Mountain, Sky, and Cocoon:\n\n- **Mountain:** Add `folders` array inline to WorkspaceDTO in InitData so extensions reading `vscode.workspace.workspaceFolders` synchronously (vscode.git, gitlens, typescript) see real folders immediately instead of `[]`. Also add `configuration` field for workspace config path. Enable CWD-autoload by default in debug builds to support git repository scanning.\n\n- **Sky:** Remove custom fallback status bar that was overlaying VS Code's native `.statusbar`. Extension-contributed status bar items now display properly through the native mechanism. Add SCM event bridge handlers that dispatch `cel:scm:*` CustomEvents when Mountain emits `sky://scm/{register,unregister,updateGroup}`.\n\n- **Cocoon:** Submodule pointer update.\n\nImpact: Extensions like vscode.git and gitlens now surface tree-views on cold boot in debug builds. SCM state events properly route to Sky-side consumers.",
			"SHA": "57037f91c30cb6ae84bcd0ca48ddbeb7a21a1ccb"
		}
